     specimen. A blunter root reduces triaxial constraint at the crack tip, so more
     plastic work is done before fracture even though the ligament is smaller
     (mild steel: KV ~ 27 J vs KU ~ 40 J is the classic textbook pair). The effect
     fades to 1.0 as the material becomes brittle — a cleavage fracture is
     comparatively insensitive to notch acuity. */
