  /* The machine artwork is drawn in its own fixed coordinate system and then
     mapped into the canvas by ONE uniform transform (see fitMachine()). That
     keeps every existing constant — anvils, vice, dial, insets — untouched
     while guaranteeing the whole pendulum swing is on screen.

     Why it was needed: the pivot sits at (250, 95) with a 340 px arm, so the
     raised hammer landed at y = -199 at alpha = 150 deg. At EVERY alpha in the
     90-160 range the hammer was off-canvas, and at 150 deg only 30 % of the arm
     was visible — so changing alpha appeared to do nothing. */
